# 🎨 Learn Component Library Documentation

**🚨 CRITICAL: USE EXISTING WIDGETS ONLY**

**Before creating ANY new widget, container, card, or UI component:**
1. **Search this library first** - 90% of what you need already exists
2. **Adapt existing widgets** - Customize props instead of building from scratch
3. **Only create new widgets** if absolutely no existing component can be adapted
4. **Keep the app consistent** - Reusing widgets ensures visual consistency

**Goal:** Every screen should look like it belongs to the same app. Use the same cards, buttons, dialogs, and patterns everywhere.

---

## 📁 Widget Organization

All widgets are organized in `/lib/core/widgets/` by category:

```
lib/core/widgets/
  ├── actions/          → Action buttons
  ├── animations/       → Animated components
  ├── borders/          → Border styles
  ├── buttons/          → Button components
  ├── cards/            → Card components (MOST USED)
  ├── dialogs/          → Bottom sheets, modals, dialogs
  ├── display/          → Headers, banners, text displays
  ├── domain_specific/  → Feature-specific widgets
  ├── empty_states/     → Empty state components
  ├── inputs/           → Search bars, dropdowns, filters
  ├── layout/           → Layout helpers
  ├── list/             → List items and sections
  ├── loading/          → Loading indicators
  ├── navigation/       → Navigation components
  ├── project_specific/ → App-level widgets
  └── user_tour/        → User tour system
```

