## 🎨 Display Components

**Location:** `lib/core/widgets/display/`

### 1. `AppPremiumHeader` ⭐ USE FOR ALL PAGE HEADERS
**Replace AppBar with this**

```dart
import 'package:learn/core/widgets/display/app_premium_header.dart';
```

---

#### ✅ **Recommended: Structured Parameters** (Use this 95% of the time)

Creates a beautiful cascading text header with consistent styling:

```dart
// In CustomScrollView:
slivers: [
  AppPremiumHeader(
    title: 'Page Title', // Required for accessibility
    headerImageUrl: AppHeaders.courses,
    showBackButton: true,
    onBack: () => Navigator.pop(context),
    // Structured content - automatically styled!
    contextIcon: SvgIcons.courses(size: 16, color: colorScheme.primary),
    contextLabel: 'Course Management',
    achievementTitlePrimary: 'Add a New',  // Large, bold text
    achievementTitleSecondary: 'Course',   // Slightly smaller, lighter
    detailedSubtitle: 'Organize your studies by setting up a new academic course.',
    // Optional: bottom widget (search bar, buttons, etc.)
    bottomChild: AppSearchBar(onSearch: _search),
  ),
  // Rest of content...
]
```

**Automatically creates this visual hierarchy:**
1. **Context Label** (icon + small text) - "What this page is"
2. **Cascading Title** (large → medium text) - "What user wants to achieve"
3. **Subtitle** (body text) - "How they'll achieve it"

---

#### 🔧 **Advanced: Custom Content** (For unique layouts only)

If you need complete control (rare), use the `content` property:

```dart
AppPremiumHeader(
  title: 'Exam Hub',
  headerImageUrl: headerImage,
  onBack: () => Navigator.pop(context),
  content: Column(
    crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,
    children: [
      // Your completely custom layout
      // Only use when structured parameters don't fit
    ],
  ),
)
```

---

#### 📐 **Legacy: Title/Description** (Still supported)

Old API for backward compatibility:

```dart
AppPremiumHeader(
  title: 'Exam Hub',
  description: 'Find any exam',
  logoUrl: categoryLogo,
  headerImageUrl: headerImage,
  badgeIcon: Icons.library_books,
  badgeText: '500+ Exams',
  onBack: () => Navigator.pop(context),
)
```

---

**Features:**
- Premium header with image background
- Three layout modes: structured (recommended), custom (`content`), or legacy
- Automatic cascading text styling
- Logo display (circular)
- Badge support
- Search bar at bottom
- Parallax scroll effect
- Works as SliverAppBar

