## ✅ Before Creating a New Widget - Checklist

- [ ] Searched this document for similar component
- [ ] Checked `/cards/` directory
- [ ] Checked `/dialogs/` directory
- [ ] Checked `/inputs/` directory
- [ ] Checked root level widgets
- [ ] Tried adapting existing widget with different props
- [ ] Confirmed no existing widget can handle this use case
- [ ] New widget follows branding guidelines (`.cursor/rules/branding_rules.mdc`)
- [ ] New widget follows design system (`.cursor/rules/design_system.mdc`)

**Only proceed with new widget if ALL checks pass.**

---

## 🎨 Design Consistency

All widgets automatically follow:
- ✅ Material 3 color scheme
- ✅ Light/dark mode support
- ✅ Consistent spacing (4/8/12/16px)
- ✅ Standard border radius (12px cards)
- ✅ Unified typography
- ✅ SvgIcons system (never Material Icons directly)

---

**Remember:** Using existing widgets makes the app feel cohesive and professional. Every time you reuse a widget instead of creating a new one, you're improving consistency and maintainability.
